2,"text":"She heeded no voice; she accepted no correction. She does not trust in the LORD; she has not drawn near to her God.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":3,"text":"Her princes are roaring lions; her judges are evening wolves, leaving nothing for the morning.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":42,"end":45,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":4,"text":"Her prophets are reckless, faithless men. Her priests profane the sanctuary; they do violence to the law.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":5,"text":"The LORD within her is righteous; He does no wrong. He applies His justice morning by morning; He does not fail at dawn, yet the unjust know no shame.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":6,"text":"“I have cut off the nations; their corner towers are destroyed. I have made their streets deserted with no one to pass through. Their cities are laid waste, with no man, no inhabitant.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":90,"end":98,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":7,"text":"I said, ‘Surely you will fear Me and accept correction.’ Then her dwelling place would not be cut off despite all for which I punished her. But they rose early to corrupt all their deeds.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":102,"end":109,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":8,"text":"Therefore wait for Me,” declares the LORD, “until the day I rise to testify. For My decision is to gather nations, to assemble kingdoms, to pour out upon them My indignation — all My burning anger. For all the earth will be consumed by the fire of My jealousy.","notes":[{"at":76,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"3:8 LXX and Syriac; Hebrew rise up to plunder","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["3:8 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["LXX and Syriac; Hebrew "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["rise up to plunder"]}]}],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":9,"text":"For then I will restore pure lips to the peoples, that all may call upon the name of the LORD and serve Him shoulder to shoulder.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":10,"text":"From beyond the rivers of Cush My worshipers, My scattered people, will bring Me an offering.","notes":[{"at":30,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"3:10 That is, the upper Nile region","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["3:10 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["That is, the upper Nile region"]}]}],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":11,"text":"On that day you will not be put to shame for any of the deeds by which you have transgressed against Me. For then I will remove from among you those who rejoice in their pride, and you will never again be haughty on My holy mountain.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":12,"text":"But I will leave within you a meek and humble people, and they will trust in the name of the LORD.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":13,"text":"The remnant of Israel will no longer do wrong or speak lies, nor will a deceitful tongue be found in their mouths. But they will feed and lie down, with no one to make them tremble.”","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":46,"end":48,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":14,"text":"Sing for joy, O Daughter of Zion; shout aloud, O Israel! Be glad and rejoice with all your heart, O Daughter of Jerusalem!","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":15,"text":"The LORD has taken away your punishment; He has turned back your enemy. Israel’s King, the LORD, is among you; no longer will you fear any harm.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":16,"text":"On that day they will say to Jerusalem: “Do not fear, O Zion; do not let your hands fall limp.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":17,"text":"The LORD your God is among you; He is mighty to save. He will rejoice over you with gladness; He will quiet you with His love; He will rejoice over you with singing.”","notes":[{"at":126,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"3:17 Or He will be silent in His love; LXX and Syriac He will renew you with His love","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["3:17 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["Or "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["He will be silent in His love"]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["; LXX and Syriac "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["He will renew you with His love"]}]}],"characterSpans":[{"start":108,"end":111,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":18,"text":"“I will gather those among you who grieve over the appointed feasts, so that you will no longer suffer reproach.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":19,"text":"Behold, at that time, I will deal with all who afflict you. I will save the lame and gather the scattered; and I will appoint praise and fame for the disgraced throughout the earth.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":20,"text":"At that time I will bring you in; yes, at that time I will gather you. For I will give you fame and praise among all the peoples of the earth when I restore your captives before your very eyes,” says the LORD.","notes":[{"at":170,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"3:20 Or your fortunes","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["3:20 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["Or "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["your fortunes"]}]}],"characterSpans":[]}],"headings":[{"afterVerse":null,"style":"s1","text":"Judgment on Jerusalem","content":["Judgment on Jerusalem"]},{"afterVerse":5,"style":"s1","text":"Purification of the Nations","content":["Purification of the Nations"]},{"afterVerse":8,"style":"s1","text":"A Faithful Remnant","content":["A Faithful Remnant"]},{"afterVerse":13,"style":"s1","text":"Israel’s Restoration","content":["Israel’s Restoration"]}],"paragraphs":[{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":1,"start":0,"end":30}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":1,"start":31,"end":54}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":1,"start":54,"end":54},{"verse":2,"start":0,"end":20}]},{"style":"q2","spans":[{"verse":2,"start":21,"end":48}]},{"style":"q1","spans":[{"verse":2,"start":49,"end":80}]},{